    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look toward a heavy slate today, headlined by the elite offensive potential of **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29), **Jackson Merrill** (71.85), **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.38), and **Kyle Tucker** (71.33). **Gunnar Henderson** stands out as our premier play; he benefits from a double-digit boost in park factors and a favorable matchup against Buehler (4.56 xERA), compounded by wind conditions blowing out, making him a prime candidate for multi-base production. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** and **Kyle Tucker** are locked into high-ceiling outcomes, with **Jackson Merrill** utilizing his speed profile against a vulnerable Rogers, Tr matchup. While **Liam Hicks** holds down the catcher spot, his score of 42.69 is tempered significantly by facing the elite arm of Skenes, necessitating a cautious outlook for our leadoff hitter today.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved weighing **Dominic Smith** (47.21) against our active lineup; while his platoon edge provided a marginal boost, he ultimately fell short of the efficiency threshold compared to the high-OBP production projected from **Nolan Schanuel** and **Wade Meckler**. We are monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Jacob Wilson**, **Josh Jung**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Nolan Schanuel** closely; should any of these bats fall out of their assumed spots in the top half of the order, their efficiency scores\u2014and our reliance on them for the day\u2014will fluctuate accordingly. **Nasim Nunez** provides a distinct SB threat despite a lower 52.98 score, as his speed is essential to mitigating the risk of the \"Elite Hold\" SP Hancock. We are proceeding with the current configuration to maximize our 5x5 categories, while continuing to roster the sidelined **Luis Robert Jr.** on the IL, hoping for his eventual return to solidify our outfield depth.",
